{"arrivo":"ru","origine":"lt","origine_nome":"Lithuanian","n":8,"parole":[{"parola":"баланда","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"skillygalee","termine_origine":"balánda","catena":[{"codice":"lt","nome":"Lithuanian","termine":"balánda","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"lt","ambiti":["mare"],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Lithuanian balánda (“orach, Atriplex spp.”). The colloquial and slang meanings are probably implying a poor taste of meal cooked with this plant."},{"parola":"вентерь","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"fyke net","termine_origine":"vénteris","catena":[{"codice":"lt","nome":"Lithuanian","termine":"vénteris","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"lt","ambiti":["mare"],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Lithuanian vénteris."},{"parola":"калба","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"the Lithuanian language","termine_origine":"kalba","catena":[{"codice":"lt","nome":"Lithuanian","termine":"kalba","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"lt","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Lithuanian kalba."},{"parola":"ковш","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"scoop, dipper, ladle","termine_origine":"káušas","catena":[{"codice":"lt","nome":"Lithuanian","termine":"káušas","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-bsl-pro","nome":"Proto-Balto-Slavic","termine":"*káuˀtei","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":["cucina"],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old East Slavic ковшь (kovšĭ), borrowed from Lithuanian káušas (“ladle, dipper, big spoon”), derived from Lithuanian káuti (“hew, chop out”), from Proto-Balto-Slavic *káuˀtei, from Proto-Indo-European *kowh₂-, from the root *kewh₂-."},{"parola":"кувшин","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"jug, pitcher","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"lt","nome":"Lithuanian","termine":"","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"ine-bsl-pro","nome":"Proto-Balto-Slavic","termine":"*káuˀtei","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":["cucina"],"via":"","testo":"From late Old East Slavic кувшинъ (kuvšinŭ), кушинъ (kušinŭ), interpreted as Lithuanian *kaušinas derived from Lithuanian káušas (“ladle, dipper, big spoon”) whence also ковш (kovš), formed from káuti (“hew, chop out”), from Proto-Balto-Slavic *káuˀtei, from Proto-Indo-European *kowh₂-, from the roo"},{"parola":"лабас","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"a Lithuanian.","termine_origine":"labas","catena":[{"codice":"lt","nome":"Lithuanian","termine":"labas","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"lt","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Lithuanian labas (“hello”), as in the greetings labas rytas (“good morning”) and labas vakaras (“good evening”)."},{"parola":"лит","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"litas (currency of Lithuania)","termine_origine":"litas","catena":[{"codice":"lt","nome":"Lithuanian","termine":"litas","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"lt","ambiti":["finanza"],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Lithuanian litas."},{"parola":"янтарь","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"amber (fossil resin)","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"lt","nome":"Lithuanian","termine":"","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"lt","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Middle Russian ꙗнтарь (jantarʹ), from earlier онтарь (ontarʹ), оньтарь (onʹtarʹ). Borrowed from Lithuanian, dialectal jentaras, gẽntaras, literary giñtaras, gintãras."}]}